From: wilkbook packaging
Subject: build: make prewarmer Linux headers explicit

This is a build-environment adaptation, not a gVisor runtime fix.  The
freestanding prewarmer is a genrule that invokes $(CC) directly, outside the
normal C/C++ compile actions, and therefore does not receive the configured
toolchain's include search flags.  The Guix package supplies the matching
target Linux UAPI headers through the strict action environment.

--- a/runsc/prewarmer/BUILD
+++ b/runsc/prewarmer/BUILD
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ genrule(
     name = "gvisor-sentry-prewarmer",
     srcs = ["prewarmer.c"],
     outs = ["gvisor-sentry-prewarmer"],
-    cmd = "$(CC) $(CC_FLAGS) " +
+    cmd = "$(CC) $(CC_FLAGS) $$GVISOR_PREWARMER_INCLUDE_FLAGS " +
           "-Os " +
           "-ffreestanding " +
           "-fno-sanitize=all " +
